# Week 6 Learning Journal – Team Project Setup

**Date:** 18 July 2026

## Overview

This week focused on setting up our team project and preparing the collaboration tools that we will use throughout the semester. Our team organised our communication channels, project repository, and project management board to ensure everyone could work together efficiently.

## What I Learned

During this week's activities, I learned how to use several collaboration tools for software development:

- Joined the team's Discord server for communication.
- Connected with my teammates on LinkedIn.
- Joined the GitHub Classroom repository for version control.
- Accessed the team's Trello board for project planning and task management.
- Learned how these tools work together to support teamwork and software development.

I also gained a better understanding of the importance of communication, version control, and project planning in a team environment.

## Practical Work

This week I completed the following tasks:

- Joined my team's Discord server.
- Connected with my teammates on LinkedIn.
- Joined the GitHub repository.
- Accessed and reviewed the team's Trello board.
- Read the project requirements and group agreement.
- Discussed the project plan with my teammates.

These tools will help our team communicate effectively, organise tasks, and manage project progress throughout the semester.

## Challenges

One challenge was learning how to use several collaboration platforms together. I had limited experience with GitHub and Trello, so I spent some time understanding how to manage project files, create tasks, and monitor project progress.

After completing the setup process, I became more confident using these tools and understood how they support collaborative software development.

## Reflection

This week's activities showed me that successful software development requires more than programming skills. Good communication, clear task management, and effective version control are all essential when working in a team.

I now feel more prepared for the group project and understand how Discord, GitHub, and Trello can improve collaboration and project organisation.

